n complex that participates in mRNA degradation. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>1661</fpage>&#x02013;1671.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10747033</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Brummelkamp, T.R., R. Bernards, and R. Agami. <year>2002</year>. A system for stable expression of short interfering RNAs in mammalian cells. <source>Science.</source> <volume>296</volume>:<fpage>550</fpage>&#x02013;553.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11910072</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Buhler, M., M.F. Wilkinson, and O. Muhlemann. <year>2002</year>. Intranuclear degradation of nonsense codon-containing mRNA. <source>EMBO Rep.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>646</fpage>&#x02013;651.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12101097</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Butler, J.S. <year>2002</year>. The yin and yang of the exosome. <source>Trends Cell Biol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>90</fpage>&#x02013;96.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11849973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Caponigro, G., and R. Parker. <year>1996</year>. Mechanisms and control of mRNA turnover in <italic>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</italic>. <source>Microbiol. Rev.</source> <volume>60</volume>:<fpage>233</fpage>&#x02013;249.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8852902</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Chen, C.Y., R. Gherzi, S.E. Ong, E.L. Chan, R. Raijmakers, G.J. Pruijn, G. Stoecklin, C. Moroni, M. Mann, and M. Karin. <year>2001</year>. AU binding proteins recruit the exosome to degrade ARE-containing mRNAs. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>107</volume>:<fpage>451</fpage>&#x02013;464.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11719186</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Chen, J., Y.C. Chiang, and C.L. Denis. <year>2002</year>. CCR4, a 3&#x02032;-5&#x02032; poly(A) RNA and ssDNA exonuclease, is the c